    "title_en": "An improved direct limit on the muon electric dipole moment",
    "abstract_en": "A limit on the permanent electric dipole moment (EDM) of the positive muon is presented based on data from the Fermilab Muon g-2 Experiment taken between 2019 and 2020. The tracking detectors measure the average vertical decay angle of positrons from muon decays, enabling a search for an interaction between a possible muon EDM $d_μ$ and the lab-frame magnetic field. The result, $d_μ= (-0.35 \\pm 0.19_{\\mathrm{stat}} \\pm 0.34_{\\mathrm{sys}}) \\times10^{-19}~e\\cdot$cm, is consistent with zero and sets a new direct limit on the muon EDM of $|d_μ|<1.10\\times10^{-19}~e\\cdot$cm at the 95 percent confidence level.",
